  "id": "COMPOUND:37977 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,4aS,6S,8aS)-4,8a-dimethyl-6-[(2R)-6-methyl-4-oxohept-5-en-2-yl]-2-oxo-1,4a,5,6,7,8-hexahydronaphthalen-1-yl] acetate is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways. It is a target of HCC1599, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including Biondinin D, (24R)-24,25-Epoxysunpollenol, and Dibutyl Oxalate. All of these compounds are linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the polycomb group (PcG) proteins. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially through a direct or indirect interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in targeting the PcG complex, possibly through a mechanism involving the inhibition or regulation of its activity.",
